**BUG-102: Stock disappears after a failed order**
In createOrder, the reserve loop happens before checking whether all lines can be reserved. Need to reserve all lines first (or check beforehand). The spec says "If any line cannot be reserved, the order is rejected with InventoryError and no stock at all remains reserved for that attempt — including lines that were reserved successfully before the failing one."

So the fix: collect all lines, try to reserve them all in a transaction-like manner. If any fails, rollback (release the ones already reserved). Or better: first check availability of all lines, then reserve all.

```js
createOrder:
  ...
  // Check availability first
  for (const l of merged) {
    if (this.inventory.available(l.sku) < l.qty) throw new InventoryError(...);
  }
  // Now reserve all
  for (const l of merged) this.inventory.reserve(l.sku, l.qty);
```

This way, if any line fails the availability check, no stock is reserved.

